    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2003-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The product is \\[1! \\cdot 2! \\cdots 9! = 2^{30}\\cdot3^{13}\\cdot5^{5}\\cdot7^{3}.\\]\n\nA perfect-square divisor has the form \\(2^{2a}3^{2b}5^{2c}7^{2d}\\) with \\(0\\le a\\le15,\\) \\(0\\le b\\le6,\\) \\(0\\le c\\le2,\\) and \\(0\\le d\\le1.\\)\n\nThe number of choices is \\(16\\cdot7\\cdot3\\cdot2=672.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the factorials into \\(2^{30}\\cdot3^{13}\\cdot5^{5}\\cdot7^{3}\\)",
        "A square divisor uses an even exponent of each prime"
      ],
